cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "codedfade: coded free-space-optical link performance over temporally correlated fading"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Interleaver depth as the primary design variable for a coded free-space-optical
  link over a temporally correlated fading channel. Lognormal and gamma-gamma
  amplitude fading generated as filtered-Gaussian sample paths, so fade duration is
  an emergent property of the model; Reed-Solomon and convolutional coding
  implemented in-package; block and convolutional interleaving with the latency and
  memory cost of every depth; a hardware abstraction layer with a simulated and a
  contract-only device backend sharing one test suite; and a learned
  fade-duration-exceedance predictor benchmarked against the level-crossing-rate
  analytic baseline. Research-grade; not flight-qualified, not certified, not
  approved for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - free-space optical communication
  - atmospheric turbulence
  - scintillation
  - gamma-gamma fading
  - Reed-Solomon
  - interleaving
  - level-crossing rate
  - fade duration
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/codedfade"
